      "imageUrl": "https://simkl.in/episodes/50/50772433f0283c607_w.webp",
      "description": "Both teams manage to take a set each as they start the third set. Since they were able to stop Ushijima, Karasuno tries to stay on that wave. But Shiratorizawa`s setter, Shirabu, seems unfazed by the loss of the second set and they are shown why they`re called undefeated champions. Meanwhile, Ushijima says something to Hinata and..."
    },
    {
      "episode": 6,
      "episodeNumber": 6,
      "title": "The Chemical Change of Encounters",
      "aired": "2016-11-12T01:55:00+09:00",
      "airedDate": "2016-11-12T01:55:00+09:00",
      "thumbnail": "https://simkl.in/episodes/50/509539382f099abf0_w.webp",
      "imageUrl": "https://simkl.in/episodes/50/509539382f099abf0_w.webp",
      "description": "Shiratorizawa quickly takes a second set, so Karasuno is now out of chances. However, Hinata ups his defense and the two teams battle it out even more intensely. It seems that things are picking back up for Karasuno, when Kageyama..."
    },
    {
      "episode": 7,
      "episodeNumber": 7,
      "title": "Obsession",
      "aired": "2016-11-19T01:55:00+09:00",
      "airedDate": "2016-11-19T01:55:00+09:00",
      "thumbnail": "https://simkl.in/episodes/51/5114441653b713530_w.webp",
      "imageUrl": "https://simkl.in/episodes/51/5114441653b713530_w.webp",
      "description": "The match finally reaches the final set, which will be won by whoever gets 15 points first. Keishin sees that Kageyama is exhausted, and switches him out with Sugawara. Sugawara had always only done attacks that he knew would work for sure, but after the Tokyo training camp..."
    },
    {
      "episode": 8,
      "episodeNumber": 8,
      "title": "An Annoying Guy",
      "aired": "2016-11-26T01:55:00+09:00",
      "airedDate": "2016-11-26T01:55:00+09:00",
      "thumbnail": "https://simkl.in/episodes/51/513572320f851688c_w.webp",
      "imageUrl": "https://simkl.in/episodes/51/513572320f851688c_w.webp",
      "description": "Because Tsukishima`s hand was injured, Karasuno`s block isn`t as strong, so they decide to go after Shiratorizawa with forceful attacks. Meanwhile, Hinata`s play finally makes Ushijima feel like he`s worth playing against."
    },
    {
      "episode": 9,
      "episodeNumber": 9,
      "title": "The Volleyball Idiots",
      "aired": "2016-12-03T01:55:00+09:00",
      "airedDate": "2016-12-03T01:55:00+09:00",
      "thumbnail": "https://simkl.in/episodes/51/51517250d99d93ea5_w.webp",
      "imageUrl": "https://simkl.in/episodes/51/51517250d99d93ea5_w.webp",
      "description": "Shiratorizawa gets a match point, which puts Karasuno in a very difficult position, but then Tsukishima manages to come back. All of the players are at the end of their ropes, but they continue to give their all to the last part of the match!"
    },
    {
      "episode": 10,
      "episodeNumber": 10,
      "title": "The Battle of Concepts",
      "aired": "2016-12-10T01:55:00+09:00",
      "airedDate": "2016-12-10T01:55:00+09:00",
      "thumbnail": "https://simkl.in/episodes/51/5170327775d8bc67f_w.webp",
      "imageUrl": "https://simkl.in/episodes/51/5170327775d8bc67f_w.webp",
      "description": "The score of the final set finally enters the 20`s. Shiratorizawa shows off individual strengths, and Karasuno continues to be reckless. Despite their methods being different, this is a battle between very similar teams.\nWho will win in the end?"
